IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`

-- Israel: the defined terms of s 3 of the Interpretation Law 5741-1981, as functions that say what falls within each term.
--
-- s 3 lists 26 entries; "day", "year and month" and "fiscal year" are in il-interpretation-time.l4 (pass 1) and the other
-- 23 are here. Each entry is a function over a small typed representation of the thing the word is asked of, built from the
-- facts the entry itself names (what it includes, what it excludes, what it points at):
--   * "includes" (לרבות) extends the ordinary meaning, so the ordinary meaning is a plain input (a judgement);
--   * a plain "means" (משמעו / dash) is exhaustive, so there is no such input;
--   * an entry that points at another Act that is not among the sources (the Penal Law) asks the pointed-at fact as an input;
--   * an entry that points at another entry of s 3 calls that entry's function.
-- FALSE, below, always means "the thing is not within the term".
-- The last function is the opening words of s 3: which of these entries govern the words of an enactment given on a day.
-- Source: the unofficial Wikisource consolidation, ../../source/law.wiki (src:N). English glosses are mine; the Hebrew governs.

§ `Interpretation Law s 3: the defined terms`

§§ `Nouns`

-- What a statute is (entries "statute" and "ordinance").
DECLARE `A candidate statute` HAS
    `passed by the Knesset as a law`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- An instrument that might be a statute, a regulation, an enactment or an administrative direction.
DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `taken as a statute`                                   IS A `A candidate statute`
    `the statute it was given by virtue of`                IS A MAYBE `A candidate statute`
    `of legislative effect`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `given in writing`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a direction or appointment, or a notice, announcement, licence, permit or the like`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a direction`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appointment`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a notice`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `an announcement`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a licence`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a permit`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `something like them`                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "law" (דין): what may be a law.
DECLARE `A source that may be law` IS ONE OF
    `an instrument` HAS `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
    `religious law, oral or written` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `oral religious law` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `written religious law` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an Act of the British Parliament, an Order in Council or part of either, or regulations under them` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an Act of the British Parliament or part of it` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an Order in Council or part of it` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulations under an Act of the British Parliament or an Order in Council` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the common law and the principles of equity of England` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the common law of England` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the principles of equity of England` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Ottoman law` HAS `in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any other source`

-- Entry "in writing" (בכתב).
DECLARE `A presentation of letters, numerals or signs` HAS
    `it is writing in the ordinary sense`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it presents letters, numerals or signs`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a form visible to the eye`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a form capable of being decoded visually`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it presents letters`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it presents numerals`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it presents signs`                                            IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "breach" (הפרה).
DECLARE `Conduct towards a requirement or direction` IS ONE OF
    `doing what it forbids`
    `not complying with it`
    `complying with it`

-- Entry "final" (חלוט).
DECLARE `A judgment or decision` HAS
    `it is a judgment or decision of a court`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appeal, objection or the like still lies against it`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appeal still lies against it`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appeal by petition still lies against it`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `an objection still lies against it`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a like remedy still lies against it`                              IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "district" (מחוז).
DECLARE `A division of the State's area` HAS
    `it is an administrative district`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the area of the State is divided into it by the Government`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the division is made by virtue of`                          IS A `A candidate statute`

-- Entries "movables" (מיטלטלין) and "immovables" (מקרקעין).
DECLARE `A thing of property` HAS
    `it is tangible`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is ground`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is built on ground`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is planted in ground`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is attached to ground permanently`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a detachable fixture`                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "coastal waters" (מימי חופין).
DECLARE `A point at sea` HAS
    `it is in the open sea along the coast of the State`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `its distance seaward from the low-water point on the shore, in nautical miles`     IS A NUMBER

-- Entry "representative of the Attorney General" (נציג היועץ המשפטי לממשלה).
DECLARE `A person who may represent the Attorney General` HAS
    `a prosecutor in the State Attorney's Office, including its branches`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by the Attorney General to be his representative or agent`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "determined" (נקבע).
DECLARE `Where something was determined` IS ONE OF
    `in the enactment in which the expression appears`
    `in regulations made under that enactment`
    `somewhere else`

-- Entry "consul" (קונסול).
DECLARE `A consular post` IS ONE OF
    `a consul general`
    `a consul`
    `a vice-consul`
    `one authorised to fill the function of one of these`
    `a consular agent`
    `any other post`

-- Entry "local authority" (רשות מקומית).
DECLARE `A local body` IS ONE OF
    `a municipality`
    `a local council`
    `a local committee`
    `a union of towns`
    `any other body`

-- Entry "corporation" (תאגיד).
DECLARE `A body` HAS
    `it is a legal body`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is capable of obligations`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is capable of rights`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is capable of legal acts`                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "possession" (תפישה), in relation to land.
DECLARE `A holding of land` HAS
    `it is possession in the ordinary sense`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is use, possession or enjoyment`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is as an employee or official only`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is for supervision or guarding only`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is use`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is possession`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is enjoyment`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- Entry "affidavit" (תצהיר).
DECLARE `A declaration` HAS
    `it is a declaration in writing`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was given`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was verified in one of the ways an enactment fixes for it`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- The opening words of s 3: the entries, one constructor each ("year" and "month" are separate words of one entry).
DECLARE `An entry of section 3` IS ONE OF
    `the entry on "in writing"`
    `the entry on "law"`
    `the entry on "administrative direction"`
    `the entry on "breach"`
    `the entry on "statute"`
    `the entry on "sin"`
    `the entry on "enactment"`
    `the entry on "final"`
    `the entry on "day"`
    `the entry on "district"`
    `the entry on "movables"`
    `the entry on "coastal waters"`
    `the entry on "immovables"`
    `the entry on "representative of the Attorney General"`
    `the entry on "determined"`
    `the entry on "misdemeanour"`
    `the entry on "felony"`
    `the entry on "ordinance"`
    `the entry on "consul"`
    `the entry on "local authority"`
    `the entry on "year"`
    `the entry on "month"`
    `the entry on "fiscal year"`
    `the entry on "corporation"`
    `the entry on "possession"`
    `the entry on "affidavit"`
    `the entry on "regulation"`

§§ `Entries that point at the Penal Law, 5737-1977 (not among the sources): the pointed-at fact is an input`

-- src:40 | ”חטא“ – כהגדרתו
-- src:40 | בחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "sin" (src:40)
GIVEN `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a sin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "sin" — the breach is a sin, as the Penal Law defines it:` `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a sin` MEANS
    `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a sin`

-- src:52 | ”עוון“ – כהגדרתו
-- src:52 | בחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "misdemeanour" (src:52)
GIVEN `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a misdemeanour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "misdemeanour" — the offence is a misdemeanour, as the Penal Law defines it:` `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a misdemeanour` MEANS
    `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a misdemeanour`

-- src:53 | ”פשע“ – כהגדרתו
-- src:53 | בחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "felony" (src:53)
GIVEN `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a felony` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "felony" — the offence is a felony, as the Penal Law defines it:` `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a felony` MEANS
    `the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines it as a felony`

-- Where the meaning of a pointer entry is found. Sin, misdemeanour and felony are "as the Penal Law, 5737-1977, defines" them: the
-- Penal Law is not among the sources, so the meaning is named, not carried (the facts it settles are the inputs above).
DECLARE `Where the meaning of a word of section 3 is found` IS ONE OF
    `section 3 itself`
    `the Penal Law, 5737-1977`

-- src:40 | ”חטא“ – כהגדרתו
-- src:40 | בחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977;
-- src:52 | ”עוון“ – כהגדרתו
-- src:52 | בחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977;
-- src:53 | ”פשע“ – כהגדרתו
-- src:53 | בחוק העונשין, התשל״ז–1977;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "sin", "misdemeanour" and "felony" (where their meanings are found) (src:40-53)
GIVEN entry IS AN `An entry of section 3`
GIVETH A `Where the meaning of a word of section 3 is found`
`s 3 — where the meaning of the entry is found:` entry MEANS
    CONSIDER entry
    WHEN `the entry on "sin"`            THEN `the Penal Law, 5737-1977`
    WHEN `the entry on "misdemeanour"`   THEN `the Penal Law, 5737-1977`
    WHEN `the entry on "felony"`         THEN `the Penal Law, 5737-1977`
    OTHERWISE                                 `section 3 itself`

§§ `Entries about instruments: ordinance, statute, regulation, enactment, administrative direction, law`

-- src:54 | ”פקודה“ – פקודה שניתנה לפני הקמת המדינה או פקודה של מועצת המדינה הזמנית;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "ordinance" (src:54)
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate statute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "ordinance" — the candidate is an ordinance:` c MEANS
       c's `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State`
    OR c's `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State`

-- src:39 | ”חוק“ – חוק של הכנסת או פקודה;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "statute" (src:39)
GIVEN c IS A `A candidate statute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "statute" — the candidate is a statute:` c MEANS
       c's `passed by the Knesset as a law`
    OR `s 3 "ordinance" — the candidate is an ordinance:` c

-- src:62 | ”תקנה“ – הוראה שניתנה מכוח חוק והיא בת־פעל תחיקתי.
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "regulation" (src:62)
-- "A direction given by virtue of a statute, and of legislative effect." The statute it was given by virtue of is
-- itself asked of the entry "statute".
GIVEN i IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "regulation" — the instrument is a regulation:` i MEANS
        i's `of legislative effect`
    AND CONSIDER i's `the statute it was given by virtue of`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST c  THEN `s 3 "statute" — the candidate is a statute:` c

-- src:41 | ”חיקוק“ – חוק או תקנה;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "enactment" (src:41)
GIVEN i IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "enactment" — the instrument is an enactment:` i MEANS
       `s 3 "statute" — the candidate is a statute:` (i's `taken as a statute`)
    OR `s 3 "regulation" — the instrument is a regulation:` i

-- src:37 | ”הוראת מינהל“ – הוראה או מינוי – לרבות הודעה, מודעה, רשיון, היתר וכיוצא באלה – שניתנו בכתב מכוח חוק ואינם בני־פעל תחיקתי;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "administrative direction" (src:37)
GIVEN i IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "administrative direction" — the instrument is an administrative direction:` i MEANS
        (   i's `a direction or appointment, or a notice, announcement, licence, permit or the like`
         OR i's `a direction`
         OR i's `an appointment`
         OR i's `a notice`
         OR i's `an announcement`
         OR i's `a licence`
         OR i's `a permit`
         OR i's `something like them`)
    AND i's `given in writing`
    AND CONSIDER i's `the statute it was given by virtue of`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST c  THEN `s 3 "statute" — the candidate is a statute:` c
    AND NOT i's `of legislative effect`

-- src:32 | ”דין“ – כל אחד מאלה:
-- src:33 | (1) חיקוק;
-- src:34 | (2) דינים דתיים – בין שבעל פה ובין שבכתב – כפי תקפם במדינה;
-- src:35 | (3) (א) אקט של הפרלמנט הבריטי או דבר המלך במועצתו או חלק מהם, או תקנות לפיהם, ודיני המשפט המקובל ועקרוני היושר של אנגליה, כפי תקפם במדינה;
-- src:36 | (ב) דינים עותומניים כפי תקפם במדינה;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "law" (stem and limbs (1), (2), (3)(a), (3)(b)) (src:32-36)
-- Limb (1) is an enactment; limbs (2), (3)(a) and (3)(b) are the other sources, "as in force in the State".
-- The entry is closed ("each of these"), so a source it does not list answers FALSE (`any other source`); it is the Ordinance's
-- open entry that refuses there. Each member of a list is a constructor of its own beside the phrase as printed.
GIVEN source IS A `A source that may be law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "law" — the source is law:` source MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `an instrument` i                                     THEN `s 3 "enactment" — the instrument is an enactment:` i
    WHEN `religious law, oral or written` inForce              THEN inForce
    WHEN `oral religious law` inForce                          THEN inForce
    WHEN `written religious law` inForce                       THEN inForce
    WHEN `an Act of the British Parliament, an Order in Council or part of either, or regulations under them` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `an Act of the British Parliament or part of it` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `an Order in Council or part of it` inForce           THEN inForce
    WHEN `regulations under an Act of the British Parliament or an Order in Council` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `the common law and the principles of equity of England` inForce THEN inForce
    WHEN `the common law of England` inForce                   THEN inForce
    WHEN `the principles of equity of England` inForce         THEN inForce
    WHEN `Ottoman law` inForce                                 THEN inForce
    WHEN `any other source`                                    THEN FALSE

§§ `Entries about writing, breach and finality`

-- src:31 | ”בכתב“ – לרבות בכל דרך אחרת של הצגת אותיות, ספרות או סימנים בצורה הנראית לעין או הניתנת לפענוח חזותי;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "in writing" (src:31)
GIVEN p IS A `A presentation of letters, numerals or signs`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "in writing" — the presentation counts as writing:` p MEANS
       p's `it is writing in the ordinary sense`
    OR (    (   p's `it presents letters, numerals or signs`
             OR p's `it presents letters`
             OR p's `it presents numerals`
             OR p's `it presents signs`)
        AND (   p's `in a form visible to the eye`
             OR p's `in a form capable of being decoded visually`))

-- src:38 | ”הפרה“, לענין דרישה או הוראה – אף אי־קיומה במשמע;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "breach" (src:38)
GIVEN `the thing is a requirement or direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      conduct IS A `Conduct towards a requirement or direction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "breach" — the conduct is a breach, the thing being a requirement or direction:` `the thing is a requirement or direction` `, the conduct being` conduct MEANS
        `the thing is a requirement or direction`
    AND CONSIDER conduct
        WHEN `doing what it forbids`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `not complying with it`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `complying with it`       THEN FALSE

-- src:42 | ”חלוט“, לענין פסק דין או החלטה של בית משפט – שאין עליהם עוד ערעור או ערר או השגה כיוצא בהם;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "final" (src:42)
GIVEN j IS A `A judgment or decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "final" — the judgment or decision is final:` j MEANS
        j's `it is a judgment or decision of a court`
    AND NOT (   j's `an appeal, objection or the like still lies against it`
             OR j's `an appeal still lies against it`
             OR j's `an appeal by petition still lies against it`
             OR j's `an objection still lies against it`
             OR j's `a like remedy still lies against it`)

§§ `Entries about places and property`

-- src:44 | ”מחוז“ – אחד המחוזות המינהליים ששטח המדינה מחולק להם בידי הממשלה על פי חוק;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "district" (src:44)
GIVEN x IS A `A division of the State's area`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "district" — the division is a district:` x MEANS
        x's `it is an administrative district`
    AND x's `the area of the State is divided into it by the Government`
    AND `s 3 "statute" — the candidate is a statute:` (x's `the division is made by virtue of`)

-- src:47 | ”מימי חופין“ – רצועת ים פתוח לאורך חופי המדינה, ברוחב שנים עשר מילים ימיים מנקודת שפל המים שבחוף;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "coastal waters" (src:47)
-- "Of a width of twelve nautical miles from the low-water point on the shore": a point is within the strip if it is in
-- the open sea along the coast and no further out than twelve nautical miles. The outer edge itself is taken as
-- inside the strip (a fork, see NOTES.md, F29).
GIVEN p IS A `A point at sea`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "coastal waters" — the point is within the coastal waters:` p MEANS
        p's `it is in the open sea along the coast of the State`
    AND p's `its distance seaward from the low-water point on the shore, in nautical miles` AT LEAST 0
    AND p's `its distance seaward from the low-water point on the shore, in nautical miles` AT MOST 12

-- src:49 | ”מקרקעין“ – קרקע, כל הבנוי עליה והנטוע בה וכל דבר אחר המחובר אליה חיבור של קבע, זולת מחוברים הניתנים להפרדה;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "immovables" (src:49)
-- Ground, what is built on it and what is planted in it, and anything else attached to it permanently, "except
-- detachable fixtures". READING TAKEN (fork F27): the exception qualifies the last limb, the things "attached", which
-- is where it stands; a thing built on the ground or planted in it is immovable whether or not it could be detached.
GIVEN t IS A `A thing of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "immovables" — the thing is immovable:` t MEANS
       t's `it is ground`
    OR t's `it is built on ground`
    OR t's `it is planted in ground`
    OR (t's `it is attached to ground permanently` AND NOT t's `it is a detachable fixture`)

-- The other reading of the exception (F27): it reaches every limb, so a detachable fixture is not immovable
-- even if it is built on or planted in the ground.
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "immovables" (src:49)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "immovables" — the thing is immovable, if the exception for detachable fixtures reaches every limb:` t MEANS
        (   t's `it is ground`
         OR t's `it is built on ground`
         OR t's `it is planted in ground`
         OR t's `it is attached to ground permanently`)
    AND NOT t's `it is a detachable fixture`

-- src:46 | ”מיטלטלין“ או ”טובין“ – נכסים מוחשיים שאינם מקרקעין;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "movables" (src:46)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "movables" — the thing is movable:` t MEANS
        t's `it is tangible`
    AND NOT `s 3 "immovables" — the thing is immovable:` t

-- src:60 | ”תפישה“, לענין מקרקעין – לרבות השימוש, ההחזקה או ההנאה שלא כעובד או כפקיד בלבד או לשם השגחה או שמירה בלבד;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "possession" (src:60)
-- Includes use, possession or enjoyment "not merely as an employee or official or merely for supervision or guarding".
-- READING TAKEN (fork F28): neither exclusion may hold. "Includes" extends the ordinary meaning.
GIVEN h IS A `A holding of land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "possession" — the holding of land is possession:` h MEANS
       h's `it is possession in the ordinary sense`
    OR (    (   h's `it is use, possession or enjoyment`
             OR h's `it is use`
             OR h's `it is possession`
             OR h's `it is enjoyment`)
        AND NOT h's `it is as an employee or official only`
        AND NOT h's `it is for supervision or guarding only`)

-- The other reading (F28): "or for supervision or guarding only" is a further limb of what is included, not a second exclusion.
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "possession" (src:60)
GIVEN h IS A `A holding of land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "possession" — the holding of land is possession, if supervision or guarding is a limb of what is included:` h MEANS
       h's `it is possession in the ordinary sense`
    OR (    (   h's `it is use, possession or enjoyment`
             OR h's `it is use`
             OR h's `it is possession`
             OR h's `it is enjoyment`)
        AND NOT h's `it is as an employee or official only`)
    OR h's `it is for supervision or guarding only`

§§ `Entries about persons, bodies and offices`

-- src:50 | ”נציג היועץ המשפטי לממשלה“ או ”בא כוח היועץ המשפטי לממשלה“ – פרקליט בפרקליטות המדינה על שלוחותיה או מי שהיועץ המשפטי לממשלה הסמיכו להיות נציגו או בא־כוחו;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "representative of the Attorney General" (src:50)
GIVEN x IS A `A person who may represent the Attorney General`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "representative of the Attorney General" — the person is one:` x MEANS
       x's `a prosecutor in the State Attorney's Office, including its branches`
    OR x's `authorised by the Attorney General to be his representative or agent`

-- src:51 | ”נקבע“ – נקבע בחיקוק שבו מצוי ביטוי זה או בתקנות שניתנו לפיו;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "determined" (src:51)
GIVEN where IS A `Where something was determined`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "determined" — it was determined, being determined` where MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `in the enactment in which the expression appears`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in regulations made under that enactment`          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `somewhere else`                                    THEN FALSE

-- src:55 | ”קונסול“ או ”נציג קונסולרי“ – קונסול כללי, קונסול, סגן קונסול וכל המוסמך למלא תפקידו של אחד מאלה, וכן סוכן קונסולרי;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "consul" (src:55)
GIVEN post IS A `A consular post`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "consul" — the post is one:` post MEANS
    CONSIDER post
    WHEN `a consul general`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a consul`                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a vice-consul`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `one authorised to fill the function of one of these`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a consular agent`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other post`                                        THEN FALSE

-- src:56 | ”רשות מקומית“ – עיריה, מועצה מקומית, ועד מקומי או איגוד ערים;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "local authority" (src:56)
GIVEN body IS A `A local body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "local authority" — the body is one:` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `a municipality`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a local council`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a local committee`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a union of towns`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other body`        THEN FALSE

-- src:59 | ”תאגיד“ – גוף משפטי, כשר לחיובים, לזכויות ולפעולות משפטיות;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "corporation" (src:59)
GIVEN b IS A `A body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "corporation" — the body is a corporation:` b MEANS
        b's `it is a legal body`
    AND b's `it is capable of obligations`
    AND b's `it is capable of rights`
    AND b's `it is capable of legal acts`

-- src:61 | ”תצהיר“ – הצהרה בכתב שניתנה ואומתה באחת הדרכים הקבועות לכך בחיקוק;
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "affidavit" (src:61)
GIVEN d IS A `A declaration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 "affidavit" — the declaration is an affidavit:` d MEANS
        d's `it is a declaration in writing`
    AND d's `it was given`
    AND d's `it was verified in one of the ways an enactment fixes for it`

§§ `The opening words of s 3: which entries govern the words of an enactment given on a day`

-- src:30 | המלים והביטויים הבאים להלן – משמעותם כמפורש בצידם:
@ref Interpretation Law s 3, opening words (src:30)
-- The words of s 3 have the meaning explained beside them, subject to s 1: the Law's gate, and the rule that for an
-- enactment given before the Law only the entries s 1 and s 3 name still govern (`s 1 — section 3 applies to`, from
-- pass 1, which this calls; it is written for the eight words it lists, and every other word of s 3 is treated like
-- "day": governed only by an enactment given after the Law).
GIVEN entry IS AN `An entry of section 3`
      d IS A DATE
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3 — section 3 governs` entry `in an enactment given on` d `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (`s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word of the pass-1 list for the entry` `in an enactment given on` d)
    WHERE
        `the word of the pass-1 list for the entry` MEANS
            CONSIDER entry
            WHEN `the entry on "sin"`            THEN `the word חטא`
            WHEN `the entry on "misdemeanour"`   THEN `the word עוון`
            WHEN `the entry on "felony"`         THEN `the word פשע`
            WHEN `the entry on "fiscal year"`    THEN `the word fiscal year`
            WHEN `the entry on "coastal waters"` THEN `the word מימי חופין`
            WHEN `the entry on "year"`           THEN `the word year`
            WHEN `the entry on "month"`          THEN `the word month`
            OTHERWISE                                 `the word day`
